#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315558 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21cef8c9-92ff-5527-a837-2236a0c1f9eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown in an Equation Involving the Cross Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e2d8f49a-ac79-5aa8-9637-61fba5e4b214" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315560} {:answer/id #uuid "5898ca27-7795-55c5-846e-651f32800090" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-4,\\,5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315561} {:answer/id #uuid "5a946484-d586-5a18-bc3c-1328150dcbf0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-5,\\,4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315562} {:answer/id #uuid "25775d08-2f25-53de-a6f2-028500aa7b98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-10,\\,-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315563} {:answer/id #uuid "3d3c4a9a-0557-5dd1-9672-84ca7e477e92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4,\\,10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315564}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25775d08-2f25-53de-a6f2-028500aa7b98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-10,\\,-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315563} :answer-field/id #uuid "d340f1c0-c943-51d1-b94b-5d26117cf02a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315559}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fec673f5-a44e-512e-bccb-25dc535fa5f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-103547" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨4,x,3⟩,$ $b=⟨-2,3,0⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{181}.$ Find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 4 & x & 3 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}x & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}4 & x \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0-9)i-(0+6)j+(12+2x)k \\\\  & =⟨-9,-6,12+2x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(-9)^{2}+(-6)^{2}+(12+2x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{81+36+144+48x+4{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{261+48x+4{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{181} \\\\ \\sqrt{261+48x+4{x}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{181} \\\\ 261+48x+4{x}^{2} & =181 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}+48x+80 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+12x+20 & =0 \\\\ (x+10)(x+2) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-10,\\,-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315565 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21cef8c9-92ff-5527-a837-2236a0c1f9eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown in an Equation Involving the Cross Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a5a3a32-3ec7-5c09-8e70-b9cf5a31ac91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315567} {:answer/id #uuid "f787e2a1-a108-57d6-a197-91332c4c5fd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-1,\\,2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315568} {:answer/id #uuid "60440a4c-439d-5119-905c-67561e30bf29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2},\\,1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315569} {:answer/id #uuid "4f0cb6b0-78c4-5cee-ab00-3caf9cadda54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2},\\,2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315570} {:answer/id #uuid "c31e2fb8-44e8-5c3b-ade2-76d683db5509" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315571}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60440a4c-439d-5119-905c-67561e30bf29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2},\\,1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315569} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef892121-e7d4-5b3e-aa02-ae932bf62f5b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315566}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "02a5a42a-3364-5f22-881f-c1eb596575d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-103552" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨0,-2,3⟩,$ $b=⟨-2,1,-2x⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{53}.$ Find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2x\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2x\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2x\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(4x-3)i-(0+6)j+(0-4)k \\\\  & =⟨4x-3,-6,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(4x-3)^{2}+(-6)^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-24x+9+36+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-24x+61}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{53} \\\\ \\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-24x+61} & =\\sqrt{53} \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-24x+61 & =53 \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-24x+8 & =0 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-3x+1 & =0 \\\\ (2x-1)(x-1) & =0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2},\\,1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=\\frac{1}{2},\\,1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315572 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "733eab11-2a26-5402-8df5-bba50c9beaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cross Product Using Determinants"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fbf21181-4136-537e-8d2d-cd6d8c446fbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15i+28j+44k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315574} {:answer/id #uuid "b846f897-9a7d-5a4b-bc84-cf663e44b006" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15i-28j+32k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315575} {:answer/id #uuid "1da91ad4-4ce1-5726-9f11-ce6d5f03fd79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16i-28j+32k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315576} {:answer/id #uuid "150be567-9f83-555e-afdb-74f9c07c3ebc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15i+44j-28k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315577} {:answer/id #uuid "352ad56d-7d3d-560b-a73e-534fa709ba7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15i+28j+44k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315578}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "352ad56d-7d3d-560b-a73e-534fa709ba7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15i+28j+44k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315578} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8d0028e-63f7-5cec-b630-8a86d3257d5d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315573}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "30151494-7f54-5014-ad3c-074576b47ad0" :question/math-academy-id "q-1399" :question/problem "Let $a=8i-2j+4k$ and $b=6i+4j-\\frac{1}{2}k.$ Find $a\\times b.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 8 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 4 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 4 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}8 & -2 \\\\ 6 & 4\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(1-16)i-(-4-24)j+(32+12)k \\\\  & =-15i+28j+44k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315579 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "733eab11-2a26-5402-8df5-bba50c9beaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cross Product Using Determinants"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "903ce392-3de4-5cf7-9024-f6e05e35117c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315581} {:answer/id #uuid "af49f307-4a41-5529-9d2e-388591e89733" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315582}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "903ce392-3de4-5cf7-9024-f6e05e35117c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315581} :answer-field/id #uuid "afa9c4cf-8dd3-50ab-875e-7c5fbf54be2a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315580} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac1f7764-d896-56ec-8d8d-3228258de4f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315584}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ac1f7764-d896-56ec-8d8d-3228258de4f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315584} :answer-field/id #uuid "2531620a-1657-566e-bfa7-721a247904cc" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315583} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a4a6fe9-8ac0-5db6-8573-070e1ac368d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315586}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a4a6fe9-8ac0-5db6-8573-070e1ac368d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315586} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c66de6c-13ac-5575-9d19-c39125593efd" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315585}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "da0f8a50-e2f7-5420-bf74-24c4f1676102" :question/math-academy-id "q-275275" :question/problem "Let $u=⟨6,-2,0⟩$ and $v=⟨5,0,-3⟩.$ Find $u\\times v.$\n\n$u\\times v=⟨${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\times v & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 6 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}6 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-2)\\cdot (-3)-0\\cdot 0)i-(6\\cdot (-3)-0\\cdot 5)j+(6\\cdot 0-(-2)\\cdot 5)k \\\\  & =(6-0)i-(-18-0)j+(0-(-10))k \\\\  & =6i+18j+10k \\\\  & =⟨6,18,10⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304176 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21cef8c9-92ff-5527-a837-2236a0c1f9eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown in an Equation Involving the Cross Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4eb9364a-9cb1-566b-8666-0684d16efb9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304178}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4eb9364a-9cb1-566b-8666-0684d16efb9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304178} :answer-field/id #uuid "20e34428-29f0-542f-9d60-9a0a2f1e0f43" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304177}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b0420859-e854-5686-a566-28a8ac19b277" :question/math-academy-id "q-282270" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨x,1,2⟩,$ $b=⟨1,0,2⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{5}.$ Find $x.$\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ x & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}x & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}x & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2-0)i-(2x-2)j+(0-1)k \\\\  & =⟨2,2-2x,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(2-2x)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+(4{x}^{2}-8x+4)+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-8x+9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-8x+9} & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-8x+9 & =5 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-8x+4 & =0 \\\\ (2x-2)^{2} & =0 \\\\ 2x-2 & =0 \\\\ x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=1.$"}]}
